  "notes": "USAGE: {批判|ひはん} implies a reasoned evaluation with justification, whereas {非難|ひなん} is more about blaming or condemning without necessarily providing reasoning.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{批判|ひはん}する (to criticize)\n・{批判|ひはん}を{受|う}ける (to receive criticism)\n・{批判|ひはん}を{浴|あ}びる (to be subjected to criticism)\n・{批判|ひはん}{的|てき} (critical)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{批評|ひひょう} - literary/artistic review or critique\n・{非難|ひなん} - blame, censure (more negative)",
